{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DzRU1qsaypDeiRSPP4UzCK","type":"tool_result","content":". \"${FM_CODE_ROOT:-$REPO}/bin/lib/fm-pinned.sh\"\nfm_round_pinned worker \"$spec\" || exit 65\n# T-297: the first round on these spec bytes - a new task, or the first round\n# after a repin - reads the spec and the code, then asks or plans. A failed\n# read says first: the instructions cost less than a missed question.\nspec_first=\"$(python3 \"${FM_CODE_ROOT:-$REPO}/bin/lib/fm_first_round.py\" \"$FM_RUN_DIR\")\" || spec_first=first\n# T-302: on the self project that first round changes no file and returns one\n# plan; the next round builds only once firstmate has accepted it. Only a run\n# whose first round on these bytes wrote plan-required is held to this, so a\n# task already in flight goes on as before. FM_PLAN_FIRST=0 keeps the\n# build-first round for the suites that predate T-302 (tests/lib.sh).\nplan_mode=off; plan_state='{}'; plan_fix=''\n# T-303: the pin's door picks the path. A two-way pin has no plan round: its\n# first round builds. A one-way pin and a pin from before T-303 keep the path\n# above. T-305: an external pin written since then follows its door too, in\n# the steps firstmate owns; an older external pin keeps the one-way path.\ndoor_kind=one-way; door_reason=''; door_version=''\nif [ -n \"${FM_SPEC_PIN_JSON:-}\" ] && { [ \"$FM_EXTERNAL\" = 0 ] || jq -e 'has(\"door_lists\")' <<<\"$FM_SPEC_PIN_JSON\" >/dev/null; }; then\n  door_version=\"$(jq -r .version <<<\"$FM_SPEC_PIN_JSON\")\"\n  door_json=\"$(python3 \"${FM_CODE_ROOT:-$REPO}/bin/lib/fm_door.py\" pin <<<\"$FM_SPEC_PIN_JSON\")\" || { _fm_wip_done=1; echo \"fm-worker: the door of $TASK does not read; no round starts\" >&2; exit 65; }\n  door_kind=\"$(jq -r .kind <<<\"$door_json\")\"; door_reason=\"$(jq -r .reason <<<\"$door_json\")\"\nfi\nif [ \"$FM_EXTERNAL\" = 0 ] && [ \"${FM_PLAN_FIRST:-1}\" != 0 ] && [ \"$door_kind\" != two-way ]; then\n  if [ \"$spec_first\" = first ]; then\n    python3 -c 'import hashlib,sys; print(hashlib.sha256(open(sys.argv[1],\"rb\").read()).hexdigest())' \\\n      \"$FM_RUN_DIR/pinned/spec.json\" > \"$FM_RUN_DIR/plan-required\" || exit 70\n  fi\n  plan_state=\"$(python3 \"${FM_CODE_ROOT:-$REPO}/bin/lib/fm_plan.py\" state --run \"$FM_RUN_DIR\" \\\n    --state \"$FM_STATE_DIR\" --project \"$(fm_evidence_project)\" --task \"$TASK\" \\\n    --round \"$round_number\" --head \"$round_head\")\" || {\n    _fm_wip_done=1\n    echo \"fm-worker: the plan state of $TASK does not read; no round starts\" >&2; exit 65; }\n  plan_mode=\"$(jq -r .mode <<<\"$plan_state\")\"\n  plan_fix=\"$(jq -r '(.fix // []) | join(\", \")' <<<\"$plan_state\")\"\nfi\n# A report-only round is still the fix round its report was refused in.\n    printf '  `ASK-SPEC:%s` marker and the question to `.fm-say.md`, and change no file.\\n' \"$TASK\"\n    printf -- '- Otherwise, before you change a file, write a short plan into `.fm-say.md`:\\n'\n    printf '  the files you will change, and how you will prove the task is done. Then\\n'\n    printf '  do the work in this same round.\\n'\n  fi\n  printf '\\n---\\n\\n'\n  if [ \"$round_two\" = 1 ]; then\n    printf '\\n# This is not the first round\\n\\nYour branch already carries your earlier work. Build on it.\\n'\n  fi\n  if [ -n \"$door_version\" ]; then\n    printf '\\n# The door\\n\\nPin v%s names a %s door: %s\\n\\n' \"$door_version\" \"$door_kind\" \"$door_reason\"\n    if [ \"$door_kind\" = two-way ]; then\n      printf 'This task takes the two-way path: no plan round, so this round builds; no\\n'\n      printf 'fail-first gate; the review checks correctness and scope only, and a REJECT\\n'\n      printf 'comes back to you under the same round budget as a one-way task. CI, the scope\\n'\n      printf 'gate, the designer review of UI pages and the merge card stay. A diff that touches a\\n'\n      printf 'path on the sensitive list (the engine base list `door.base` and the project list),\\n'\n      printf 'or a path no list can classify (a new top-level path, a rename, a submodule), is\\n'\n      printf 'handled as one-way at the gates, the gate names the path, and no further round\\n'\n      printf 'starts on this pin until the captain answers its card.\\n\\n'\n      if [ \"$FM_EXTERNAL\" = 1 ]; then\n        printf 'The project keeps its own reviewers, CI and branch rules as they are.\\n\\n'\n      fi\n    else\n      printf 'This task takes the one-way path: the plan round, fail-first, the full review\\n'\n      printf 'and all six gates.\\n\\n'\n    fi\n    printf 'If this round finds evidence that the door is wrong (for example a two-way task\\n'\n    printf 'needs a data format change), write a standalone `DOOR-CHANGE:%s` line and the\\n' \"$TASK\"\n    printf 'evidence in `.fm-say.md`, and stop. No further round starts on this pin;\\n'\n    printf 'firstmate raises a new card with a revised spec.\\n'\n  fi\n  if [ \"$report_only\" = 1 ]; then\n    printf '\\n# Fix only your report\\n\\n'\n    printf 'Your last round was refused only for its report. Its changes are kept in\\n'\n    printf 'this worktree, uncommitted, and nothing was pushed. This round fixes the\\n'\n    printf 'report and changes no other file: write the whole report again into\\n'\n    printf '`.fm-say.md`. The launcher then publishes the kept changes with it. A round\\n'\n    printf 'that changes a file is refused: its changes are saved under state/rescued/\\n'\n    printf 'and the tree is put back to the kept work.\\n\\n'\n    printf 'Why it was refused: %s\\n\\n' \"$(jq -r .reason <<<\"$kept_json\")\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"568e8e5b-0eae-4721-b569-8de541c6cc51","uuid":"71ed9d68-091f-4f52-aec0-bb724f3a7c78","timestamp":"2026-10-13T16:27:42.783Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":". \"${FM_CODE_ROOT:-$REPO}/bin/lib/fm-pinned.sh\"\nfm_round_pinned worker \"$spec\" || exit 65\n# T-297: the first round on these spec bytes - a new task, or the 